A malicious app could use setAccessibilityWindowAttributes to overwrite
the accessibility title and locale of any other window by guessing its
integer windowId.

This CL adds an ownership check in AccessibilityWindowManager to ensure
that the calling UID matches the UID associated with the target window's
connection.

Verification:
1. Added unit test in AccessibilityWindowManagerTest to verify the
   SecurityException is thrown on the server side when UID mismatch
   is detected.
2. Added CTS test AccessibilityWindowMetadataTest (tagged for STS)
   to verify that foreign window attributes cannot be spoofed and
   own window attributes can still be set successfully.

